    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the Spring Boot owner API while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` string properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (min-length 1, non-blank pattern, max 255 \u2014 enforced only when present). Since `Owner` is `allOf OwnerFields`, both fields are also returned on read.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list so structured-only requests validate. The remaining required fields (`firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`) keep earlier minimal owners accepted.\n\n**Domain model** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields (mapped to new columns) with getters/setters. `address` keeps its `@NotEmpty` constraint, which now enforces the \"must supply an address in either form\" rule: it stays null (and rejects) only when neither `addressLine1` nor flat `address` is given.\n\n**Service** (`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`)\n- Replaced the flat-address normalization with `applyAddress(owner)`: it normalizes whichever address fields were supplied, and when `addressLine1` is non-blank composes the flat `address` as the normalized `addressLine1` plus a single space and normalized `addressLine2` when present; otherwise it normalizes the flat `address` in place. Because everything downstream reads `owner.getAddress()`, the household hash, postcode validation and locality all see the structured value when present and fall back to the flat address.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns to all four schemas (`hsqldb` used by tests, plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner`) \u2014 carries the two new fields through on update.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps the new fields automatically by name (no changes needed).",
